WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.001
Where is it? And which
way do you go from here?

2
00:00:07.221 --> 00:00:10.379
Today you say where things
are, and you give directions.

3
00:00:10.879 --> 00:00:14.362
Before any grid, you can say
where something is in words.

4
00:00:14.582 --> 00:00:18.018
The tree is above the boat.
The medal is below the fish.

5
00:00:18.238 --> 00:00:22.232
The boat is between the fish and
the butterfly, one on each side.

6
00:00:22.452 --> 00:00:25.378
And the star sits up
in the top left corner.

7
00:00:25.878 --> 00:00:28.943
Left and right depend on
the way you are facing.

8
00:00:29.163 --> 00:00:33.203
This robot faces the top of the
page. Its left is your left.

9
00:00:33.423 --> 00:00:37.370
Now it faces the bottom. Its
left is over on your right.

10
00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:40.795
So turn with the robot,
and never with the page.

11
00:00:41.295 --> 00:00:44.406
A turn has a size. This
much is a quarter turn.

12
00:00:44.626 --> 00:00:49.456
Two quarter turns make a half turn.
You face back the way you came.

13
00:00:49.676 --> 00:00:53.716
Four quarter turns make a whole
turn, all the way round to the start.

14
00:00:53.936 --> 00:00:58.302
A turn changes the way you face.
It does not move you along.

15
00:00:58.802 --> 00:01:03.306
Forward goes the way the robot
faces. Turn first, then go.

16
00:01:03.526 --> 00:01:07.056
The flag is two squares up,
and two squares to the right.

17
00:01:07.276 --> 00:01:10.852
The robot faces the top,
so go forward two squares.

18
00:01:11.072 --> 00:01:14.276
Now turn right. It faces
the right of the page.

19
00:01:14.496 --> 00:01:18.072
Go forward two more squares,
and it lands on the flag.

20
00:01:18.572 --> 00:01:21.358
Now you read a route that
somebody else walked.

21
00:01:21.578 --> 00:01:25.340
Start at the star, and follow
the purple trail to the flag.

22
00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:28.764
It goes two squares towards
the top of the page.

23
00:01:28.984 --> 00:01:32.560
Then it turns, and goes two
squares towards the right.

24
00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:36.170
Say how many squares, and
say which way, every time.

25
00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:40.014
A mirror line flips a shape
over to the other side.

26
00:01:40.234 --> 00:01:44.088
Look at this square. It is
two squares from the line.

27
00:01:44.308 --> 00:01:48.349
So it lands two squares away,
on the other side of the line.

28
00:01:48.569 --> 00:01:52.841
Every part flips over. The
shape does not slide across.

29
00:01:53.061 --> 00:01:56.590
The reflection is the same
size, just facing the other way.

30
00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:01.874
Position words say where something
is: above, below, between.

31
00:02:02.094 --> 00:02:05.809
Forward goes the way you
face, so turn first, then go.

32
00:02:06.029 --> 00:02:09.744
A quarter turn, a half turn, a
whole turn, all the way round.

33
00:02:09.964 --> 00:02:14.237
And a mirror line flips a shape
over, the same distance away.
